# Binary art. Without these, git sniffs a file's leading bytes and can
# decide an Illustrator .ai is TEXT — the PDF wrapper it ships inside is
# mostly ASCII — then stages a 1.3 MB working file as ~6,000 "insertions"
# and diffs it line by line on every change.
#
# The real cost is not the diff. These files carry literal NUL bytes, and
# BSD grep (the macOS default) treats a NUL-carrying file as binary: it
# exits 1 and prints NOTHING. A repo-wide search for a helper answers with
# silence rather than a match, so "not found" and "found nothing" look
# identical — the same fail-open the pre-commit hook rejects in source.
*.ai   binary
*.xcf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
